cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Evolutionary Optimization for Adaptive Cruise Control"
type: software
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: 2026-10-15
license: "GPL-3.0-only"
abstract: >-
  Research software and reproducibility package for a comparative study of
  evolutionary optimization methods applied to a three-gain Adaptive Cruise
  Control controller. The frozen V2.2-FJE formulation combines cruise-speed
  RMSE, car-following CTG-spacing RMSE, realized longitudinal jerk RMS, and
  positive tractive-energy intensity. The release includes GA, canonical DE,
  FVRADE, RNEGDE, Neighborhood-SHADE, and DE-NPS-FP implementations together
  with archived evidence for optimizer benchmarking, held-out controller
  evaluation, physical-condition sensitivity, and paired objective-term
  ablation.
